# Ralph-loop operational guardrails (this machine)

## Shell tool requires full permissions on this machine
This Windows machine cannot enforce the default `workspace_readwrite` sandbox policy (no sandbox
backend available). Every `Shell` tool call **must** pass `required_permissions: ["all"]`, otherwise
it fails immediately with "Command failed to spawn: Terminal unavailable" before running anything.
This applies to *all* shell commands here (`git`, `dotnet`, `npm`, etc.) — don't retry without it,
just always include it up front.

## Standing verification story: 177540
Work item **177540** is the controlled, dedicated ADO story created for exercising ADO_Tester
features end-to-end (QA Loop, Author Tests, Find Bugs, etc.). It is safe to write to repeatedly.

- Use story **177540** for every manual/agentic verification run during Ralph-loop task execution
  (Author Tests runs, QA Loop scans, UI-phase runs, Scripts Board executions, etc.) — never invent
  or reuse a different story/module for ad-hoc verification.
- Note: `CLAUDE.md` separately references work item **171740** as "the standing test ticket" for
  generic manual ADO checks — that is a different, older reference. For anything under the
  `qa-loop-v2` Ralph loop (and going forward, ADO_Tester feature verification generally), prefer
  **177540** per direct user instruction.
- **LLM for all verification / test runs:** always use the **ClaudeCli** provider with model
  **`haiku`** (cheap/fast; resolves to the current Haiku via Claude CLI subscription). Never run
  live agent pipelines on Sonnet/Opus for verification — set provider + `claude_cli.model` before
  starting a scan / Author Tests / Find Bugs / QA Loop UI-phase run. (Do not use Anthropic API
  unless the user explicitly asks — prefer Claude CLI + haiku.)
- After implementing each Ralph-loop task that has a runtime-verifiable surface (an endpoint, an
  orchestrator step, a UI flow), exercise it against story 177540 as part of that task's
  verification — in addition to `dotnet build`/`dotnet test`/`npm run build`/`npm run lint` — before
  flipping `[ ]` → `[x]` in `prd.md`.
- **QA Loop / Scripts Board nuance:** those two features select work by **module** (frontend route) or
  **spec file**, not by ADO story — there is no "scan story 177540" flow for them. For those features,
  target story 177540 specifically for anything that touches ADO (push a Test Case, link Tested-By, a
  Scripts Board inventory item's ADO deep link) — pick any convenient local module for the
  execution/generation part itself. Author Tests / Find Bugs (work-item-driven) always use 177540 directly.
- **ADO PAT:** live ADO verification requires a valid `ADOACCESS_PAT` in the repo-root `.env` (and a
  matching `ado.pat` runtime setting if DB overlay is present — Settings wins over `.env`). Confirm
  with `GET /api/diagnostics/workitem/177540` before ADO-touching runs; if it returns 401/502, record
  pending in `progress.md` rather than skipping the task or faking the check.
